===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sovereyn}}, from {{der|en|fro|soverain}} (whence also modern {{cog|fr|souverain}}), from {{der|en|VL.|*superānus}} (compare {{cog|it|sovrano}}, {{cog|es|soberano}}) from {{der|en|la|super||above}}. Spelling influenced by folk-etymology association with {{m|en|reign}}. {{doublet|en|soprano}}, from the same Latin root via Italian. See also {{m|en|suzerain}}, {{m|en|foreign}}.

