|passage=a '''sovereign''' remedy}}
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=Such a '''sovereign''' influence has this passion upon the regulation of the lives and actions of men.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|title=The Golden Bough|author=James George Frazer|volume=3|year=1900|page=297|text=In Spain people still bathe in the sea or roll naked in the dew of the meadows on St. John’s Eve, believing that this is a '''sovereign''' preservative against diseases of the skin.}}
